{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-truth-panel-screens-1-b-01","date":"2026-11-25","lens":"gap-9","surface":"panel","area":"panel/screens-1","refs":["F-panel-225","F-panel-202","FN-B-truth-panel-assistant-b-01"],"severity":"S4","title":"A member's page can say 'Training' in green beside a red 'Last visit 2 weeks ago', and 'Gone quiet' for someone not on the Losing the habit list","what":"The member page judges absence two ways. The Last visit box turns red after 14 days for everyone. The training label under it uses the member's own rhythm: a member who comes about once a week is only 'Slipping' after 18 days. So between day 14 and day 18 the page shows a red '2 weeks ago' next to a green 'Training'. The label also shows 'Slipping' or 'Gone quiet' for a member whose plan ended or ends within a week, while Visits > Losing the habit and its count leave that member out, with no word on the page why. And a member who paid ahead for a plan starting next week is labelled 'No plan running' right beside 'Starts in N days'.","expected":"The member page and the Losing the habit list use one rule: the red colour follows the same rhythm as the label, and when a member is left off the list because a renewal is due, the page says so (for example 'Plan ends soon: on the renewals list'). A plan paid ahead says 'Plan starts on ...', not 'No plan running'.","evidence":["apps/dashboard/src/crm/ui/screens/MemberDetail.tsx:522-527","apps/dashboard/src/crm/ui/screens/MemberDetail.tsx:983-1004","apps/dashboard/src/crm/logic/attendance.ts:403-408","apps/dashboard/src/crm/logic/attendance.ts:443-484","apps/dashboard/src/crm/logic/attendance.ts:598-601","apps/dashboard/src/crm/logic/membership.ts:385-394"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"member-page-absence-rules-differ","who":"owners and desk staff reading a member's page","how_often":"for weekly members between day 14 and 18 away, and for every quiet member whose plan is ending or not started","fix_line":"Colour Last visit by the same rhythm rule as the label, and say on the page when the member is on the renewals list instead","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
